# Prefer reusable UI controls

Before using a native HTML control (`<input type="date|time|color|file|range">`, raw `<select>`, custom checkbox/radio markup, etc.), **search `@4d/ui` first** for an existing component.

## Checklist

1. Check `packages/ui/src/index.ts` exports and existing usages in `apps/web`.
2. Prefer kit components such as `DatePicker`, `Select`, `Checkbox`, `Switch`, `RadioGroup`, `Input`, `Button`, `Dialog`.
3. Only fall back to a native control when no suitable kit component exists — and note why in the PR/commit body.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — native date input
<Input type="date" value={date} onChange={(e) => setDate(e.target.value)} />

// ✅ GOOD — shared DatePicker (locale-aware calendar)
<DatePicker value={date} onChange={setDate} locale={language} />
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — native select
<select value={v} onChange={...}>...</select>

// ✅ GOOD
<Select value={v} onValueChange={...}>...</Select>
```

